# VSCode Extension Development Rules

## Extension Lifecycle

- Implement proper activation and deactivation functions
- Use proper activation events to optimize performance
- Register commands and providers in activate function
- Dispose of resources properly in deactivate function
- Use context.subscriptions for proper cleanup

## Command Registration

- Register commands with descriptive names
- Use consistent command naming: `extension-name.commandName`
- Handle command errors gracefully
- Provide user feedback for all commands
- Use proper command categories in package.json

## Provider Development

- Implement providers for specific functionality
- Use proper disposal patterns for providers
- Handle provider errors gracefully
- Cache expensive operations when possible
- Use proper provider registration

## API Usage

- Always handle VSCode API calls properly
- Use proper error handling with user-friendly messages
- Validate editor state before operations
- Use async/await for API calls
- Follow VSCode extension API guidelines

## Performance

- Use lazy loading for heavy operations
- Minimize memory usage and avoid leaks
- Avoid blocking the main thread
- Use proper activation events
- Cache expensive operations

## User Experience

- Provide clear error messages
- Use progress indicators for long operations
- Show success messages when appropriate
- Use consistent UI patterns
- Follow VSCode UX guidelines

